    "uncited": [
     "- If $|det| < \\epsilon$, the ray is parallel to the triangle plane (or lies in it).",
     "- If $u < 0.0$ or $u > 1.0$, the intersection point lies outside the triangle edge.",
     "- If $v < 0.0$ or $u + v > 1.0$, the intersection point lies outside the triangle.",
     "- If $t < \\epsilon$ (or $t \\le 0$), the intersection is behind the ray origin or at the origin.",
     "- **Parallel Rays:** If the determinant is near zero, division by zero occurs.",
     "- **Degenerate Triangles:** If the triangle vertices are collinear, the area is zero, and the determinant may be zero or near-zero.",
     "- **Back-Facing Triangles:** The algorithm returns intersections for both front and back faces.",
     "- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per triangle.",
     "- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary space."
    ]
